From: =?UTF-8?q?Alexander=20Thei=C3=9Fen?= <alex@theissen.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:56:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] server: Complete pending polls when a connect fails
 under kqueue.

kqueue reports a failed connect as EV_EOF, which the server maps to
POLLHUP without POLLERR, and get_poll_flags() drops that on an
unconnected socket. A poll already waiting for AFD_POLL_CONNECT_ERR
then never completed.

- Report POLLERR for a failed connect

(cherry picked from commit b6ef6d11cd7788c394f135a48b0903af9c3f619d)
---
 server/sock.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/sock.c b/server/sock.c
index 0337d8d3220..bdc75dcaca0 100644
--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -1430,7 +1430,8 @@ static void sock_poll_event( struct fd *fd, int event )
         if (event & (POLLERR|POLLHUP))
         {
             sock->state = SOCK_UNCONNECTED;
-            event &= ~POLLOUT;
+            /* kqueue reports a failed connect as POLLHUP without POLLERR. */
+            event = (event & ~POLLOUT) | POLLERR;
         }
         else if (event & POLLOUT)
         {
